{"ref":"BDB, יַעֲנָה","hw":"יַעֲנָה","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">יַעֲנָה</span></big>  <strong>n.f. greed</strong>(?);—only in <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת־הַיַּעֲנָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:16\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.16\">Lv 11:16</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.15\">Dt 14:15</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנוֹת־יַעֲנָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Micah 1:8\" href=\"/Micah.1.8\">Mi 1:8</a> + 5 times;—<em>ostrich</em>, <strong>(</strong>vid. √ <span dir=\"rtl\">יען</span> supra<strong>)</strong>; as wailing (sim. of mourning) <a data-ref=\"Micah 1:8\" href=\"/Micah.1.8\">Mi 1:8</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">תַּנִּים</span>); symbol. of loneliness <a data-ref=\"Job 30:29\" href=\"/Job.30.29\">Jb 30:29</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(אָח הָיִיתִי לְתַנִּים וְרֵעַ לב׳ יַעֲ׳)</span>; of desolation, as dwelling among ruins <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 13:21\" href=\"/Isaiah.13.21\">Is 13:21</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 34:13\" href=\"/Isaiah.34.13\">34:13</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">תַּנִּים</span>), <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 50:39\" href=\"/Jeremiah.50.39\">Je 50:39</a>; living in desert <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 43:20\" href=\"/Isaiah.43.20\">Is 43:20</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">תַּנִּים</span>); unclean <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:16\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.16\">Lv 11:16</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.15\">Dt 14:15</a>.","next":"BDB, יְעֹעֵֽרוּ","prev":"BDB, יָעֵן"}